  "body": "## What was wrong\n\nTwo `innerHTML` template sinks rendered manifest-provided strings (custom-provider display_name among them) as HTML — a stored-injection path inside the loopback-only dashboard. A full audit of all 47 innerHTML sites confirmed these were the only two interpolating untrusted data.\n\n## The fix\n\nBoth sinks converted to createElement/textContent (matching renderProviderCard's existing pattern). Plus: a reusable **jsdom XSS harness** (204 lines) executing the real admin.js against malicious payloads asserting text-only rendering, a pytest contract wrapper (8 tests) so it runs in CI, and a static guard enumerating every remaining allowed `innerHTML` site. Bonus surface: renders the new `messaging_auth_open` config field as a warn notice when non-empty (companion to the messaging-auth PR).\n\n## Verification\n\nnode syntax checks; direct harness runs in open/empty modes; 8 contract tests + **32 regression tests** in the pre-existing admin jsdom suite, all green; ruff/ty clean. §66 mutations ×2 caught by name (sink reverted → injection test fails by name; notice iff-guard inverted → conditional test fails). PATCH slot **5.52.2**.\n\n## Residual risks\n\nThe docs-viewer site (~:545) intentionally keeps assigning server-rendered HTML — sanctioned allowance, now enumerated by the contract test instead of folklore.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
